, fix tooling blockers and continue every qualifying PR through successful dev merge. This text is posted by the agent exercising that delegation. It is not a newly human-authored answer, a reconstructed original user message, an independent source-review approval, a successful prerequisite-verification result, or an instruction to clear holds manually.\n\nREQUESTED AMENDMENT\n\nRequest fresh read-only planning and fresh independent review of the complete amended plan. Reassess removal of exactly the future external PR47 dev-merge prerequisite. Preserve PR47's actual inherited source, transactional renewal APIs, authority modules, tests and safeguards as mandatory baseline content. Do not remove any other prerequisite, acceptance obligation or genuine authority hold.\n\nThe old plan already pins dev 04945ba5c60f15eead12ccefdbfb4b7932284dc9. That baseline already contains PR47. No newly advanced dev base is claimed.\n\nThe actual PR47 merge is:\nrepository: Karapsin/analytics_toolkit\nPR: 47\nhead: 5ff11dc56dd5d56810a98be5838a9a5fb32d2dfc\ntask digest: 98c7370427c6332746d61e42c343c79aea0e54f3518b505c86b9258493467e51\nmerge/dev: 04945ba5c60f15eead12ccefdbfb4b7932284dc9\nprevious dev: 388b2eb738fcc8ab138ed210777d9441f400f933\nactual head/merge tree: 1e01b6c74b25d2d59ae20dae09976204ad286c5b\n\nThe coordinator's bounded inspection verified the enrolled SSH signature, successful exact-head fast-checks 118047992593, matching head/merge trees and actual current-dev inclusion. Preserve exact task/branch/signature/tree/ancestry checks and their evidence; comments or CI alone do not prove a merge.\n\nThe user separately and explicitly authorized the session's automation merge waiver:\n\"ok, just for this session, I allow you to merge any PRs which are related to automation routines witohut reviwer's approval\"\nThe user then answered the explicit protected-controller approval question:\n\"Yes, bypass both approval gates this session\"\n\nThose are the recorded owner-session instructions being quoted as authority context, not original messages newly authored by this agent. The transparent agent-authored merge execution record alone is not their authentication. Preserve the authenticated originals and their provenance.\n\nPR47's independent source review remains incomplete. Its retained execution has coverage_complete:false; the original public review remains in progress, and the later post-merge authorization-required check is not a successful review. Do not invent review approval, rewrite checks or retrospectively require an approval that the actual session waiver made unnecessary for that merge. The waiver grants no main projection, source/tag operation, runtime activation, native acceptance, visual acceptance or operational hold override.\n\nThe installed factual verifier nevertheless requires successful independent-review status. This amendment does not claim that verifier passed. Instead, commission a fresh complete plan that treats PR47 as existing mandatory implementation baseline rather than an outstanding future merge, and obtain the required independent substantive reassessment for removing that one old external condition. Bind that reassessment to this authenticated amendment's digest. The reviewer must reject removal if it merely avoids a genuinely retained requirement or drops any required PR47 feature.\n\nCURRENT INTERNAL WAIT AND QUESTION CONTEXT\n\nThere is no unanswered user question in the current wait: questions=[].\n\nThe existing structured condition is PR47 merged into dev and its recorded merge included in current dev, required before code and publication. Its recorded reason is:\n\n\"The correction must compose with PR47's authority modules, transactional renewal APIs, tests and safeguards as actual current-dev inheritance. Require its actual dev merge and inclusion of the recorded merge in current dev; source availability, CI or comments alone do not satisfy this condition. The catalogue records its merge commit as the pinned dev, subject to separate host verification.\"\n\nIts plan location is:\n\"Implementation and compatibility: preserve all incoming PR #47 authority modules, transactional renewal APIs, tests and safeguards.\"\n\nKeep that full old condition and the failed verification history in the amendment/reassessment archive. Do not relabel it as successfully verified.\n\nThe prior implementation-choice question remains settled:\n\n\"1. How should the persistent protected-conflict routing repair be owned, while preserving PR #48's receiver foundation, current-dev safeguards, and the complete parent task?\nTogether in PR48 (Recommended): Include the smallest pre-worker routing correction and fast regression with the protected conflict resolution; require fresh independent whole-plan/source review and all existing authority gates.\nSeparate automation leaf: Limit PR48 to reconciling receiver/current-dev source and history; commission a separately owned, independently reviewed routing repair PR and track both through successful dev merges.\"\n\nThe independent resolver selected Together in PR48 (Recommended). That was a scope/ownership strategy, not plan, source, protected approval, deployment permission, hold release or parent completion. Preserve the complete original answer and its resolver/audit binding; do not substitute this restatement for the original record.\n\nCOMPLETE CORRECTION PLAN TO RETAIN AND REASSESS\n\nRetain the complete current native plan, whose text SHA256 is ab38dc7de5a128b859d35550e540d2c82f7daed088258426f4f269f0d00a87aa, and every original task correction verbatim. The following restates its full implementation and validation scope for the new independent assessment. Apply the complete chronological user instructions, including the actual session waiver; historical plan text is not a new owner decision.\n\nCorrect PR48 head 573588880ad9d32afbcaa51e78844d0321a06a80 against pinned dev 04945ba5c60f15eead12ccefdbfb4b7932284dc9, preserving the receiver foundation and incoming dev features. Existing current-head fast CI and unfinished independent review do not validate the newly reconciled tree.\n\nImplementation and compatibility:\n- Reconstruct the merge in the correction workspace. Resolve conflicts by combining both features, preserving unrelated changes and leaving no conflict markers.\n- In .github/agent/controller.py retain receiver preparation and Pending publication interfaces. Include both exact protected paths: agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_render.py and .github/workflows/agent-visual-profile.yml. Preserve rename checks and deny adjacent paths.\n- Preserve all inherited PR47 authority modules, transactional renewal APIs, tests and safeguards. Retain native capture isolation, source-validation modes, diagnostic retention and workflow guards.\n- Retain dev's Python3.9+ runtime-validation matrix, minimum-dependency environment and constraints. Preserve Python3.8 public compatibility metadata and static syntax targets; do not restore obsolete Python3.8 runtime jobs.\n- Combine both operations-documentation additions and all changelog entries. Preserve receiver evidence, original task archives, questions/options/answers, historical rejections, validation history and additive metadata corrections.\n- Keep receiver wire/schema, limits, legacy scalar interfaces and purpose separation unchanged. Genuine Gate, source-operation, current-row CAS, durable history and authenticated receiver-original retrieval remain explicitly Pending. This correction implements none of those missing capabilities.\n\nPrevent the protected-conflict retry loop before worker launch:\n- Add the narrow guard inside controller preparation, immediately after the attempted dev merge and before constructing the generic conflict-worker prompt.\n- For conflict tasks inspect actual unresolved index paths using NUL-delimited Git output. Detect conflicts under the existing forbidden .github/agent/ boundary and controller-workflow path.\n- Snapshot the existing correction row before inspection. Before recording a correction reuse current publication-authority checks for pinned dev, signed head, task digest, enrollment, vetoes and owner/coordinator holds.\n- Use existing require_correction(..., expected=snapshot) semantics to durably request fresh correction planning. Preserve same-scope findings and concurrent replacement records.\n- Stop preparation before model launch. Subsequent discovery must select the existing planned-correction route, preserving the complete parent task and requiring separate plan review before coding.\n- Sensitive paths, unavailable inspection, stale authority or failed persistence refuse safely; no manufactured queued-success claim.\n- Preserve conflict-prompt restrictions, collector rejection, inherited-dev proof and publication guards. Ordinary conflicts and clean protected inheritance retain existing paths.\n- No new public API, database schema, credential permission or worker interface is required.\n\nFocused fast regressions:\n- Reproduce a real temporary-Git protected conflict with an untouched worker result; preparation must queue correction before prompt/model execution, collection or publication.\n- Verify durable restart and next discovery select correction with unchanged head/base/task bindings.\n- Cover ordinary conflicts, clean protected inheritance, deletion/rename cases and safe NUL-delimited path handling.\n- Cover changed head/dev/task, owner veto, coordinator hold, concurrent correction replacement and persistence failure; assert no push, approval, hold release or lost findings.\n- Preserve collector/publication rejection tests.\n- Require both exact protected paths and rename endpoints; reject similar paths.\n- Retain receiver HTTP/Journal, capacity, identity, lifecycle and Pending-boundary tests, plus inherited authority, isolation, source-validation and Python-profile regressions.\n\nValidation and completion:\n- Obtain fresh independent review of the complete amended correction plan against the pinned baseline and full authenticated task.\n- Implement only through the permitted source-only correction route. Within this private correction-worker invocation execute no candidate programs, tests, installs or renders locally or on the Pi. Separately authorized root Mac source-leaf checks remain distinct; they provide no private-host runtime or operational acceptance.\n- Use isolated GitHub runners for focused regressions followed by required static/type/quality, coverage, artifact and current Python compatibility checks. Preserve assertions, debt/coverage floors and aggregate failure signals.\n- Retain fresh complete composed-source/task/controller-closure assessment and exact-final-head fast CI. Apply the actual owner session waiver only within its explicit scope; do not present historical source approval or Mac checks as validation of a new head.\n- Preserve whole-controller admission, compatible consumer, main/source projection, native acceptance and operational freeze/drain gates. Source publication or dev merge does not activate the routing repair.\n- Preserve PR39/PR37 and PR10/PR9 merge/ancestry dependencies, exporter/producer-consumer gates and every 46-scene geometry/full-PNG acceptance requirement. This source-only correction provides no visual acceptance.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs until every qualifying PR and successor actually merges successfully into dev.\n\nFULL PARENT AND RECEIVER BOUNDARIES RETAINED\n\nPreserve the full signed parent archive, all four historical plans, every chronological correction, all nine resolver questions/options/answers, actual user answers, source-review rejections, original and corrected validation assessments and additive provenance. Agent-authored records remain distinguishable from human authorization. Preserve the archive-size metadata correction without rewriting the original assessment.\n\nThe receiver remains the bounded first protected source foundation: fixed strict wire/schema, purpose separation, limits and joint capacity; actual HTTP status/prefix/hash retention; abnormal open/read/close and settlement failure handling; token-taint/privacy/quarantine; immutable attempt history and no duplicate POST on uncertainty; total typed identity and exact returned-URL validation; separate later exact readback without rewriting an uncertain initial receipt; strict candidate-parent versus dev-base binding; and unchanged legacy scalar interfaces. Preserve its adversarial HTTP/Journal, capacity, identity, lifecycle, source-validation and rehearsal coverage.\n\nDo not fabricate a genuine live production Gate, source-operation issuer, current-row CAS, durable host history, authenticated receiver originals or positive interval proof. Those missing capabilities remain Pending before effects. Preserve the requirement that the actual final controller contains both root46's renderer-helper policy and the receiver-profile policy, with independently established compatible source/controller admission and consumers.\n\nPreserve capture isolation and publisher/dispatch semantics: all newly triggered candidate execution requires the reviewed isolation boundary, separate trusted transport/artifact handling, no candidate write credentials/secrets/privileged context, actual image/source/native evidence and owned cleanup. Ordinary diagnostic workflow scope and the separately owned protected capture-isolation prerequisite remain distinct. No invented publication-only or dispatch capability; no source tag/main/runtime activation follows from this amendment.\n\nPreserve every existing and unpublished SQL Explorer repair: journal warning-only failure status and recovery, exact picker heading and additive factual evidence corrections, stable parent-relative completion placement, containment/non-overlap, scrolling/resize/narrowing/lifecycle/stale-callback/insertion/dismissal behavior, fixtures, scene IDs and stress cases. Retain diagnostic-first/cause-specific planning, complete original failures/logs/provenance and meaningful negative controls. Do not infer a missing-glyph cause or silently relax assertions.\n\nKeep all46 scenes at208x47 cells with full1280x800 PNGs, every geometry assertion and independent individual full-image acceptance. Diagnostic, synthetic probe, source or transport success is not feature visual acceptance. Preserve PR39 as PR37's separate visual dependency, PR37 process-output/history obligations, exporter/producer-consumer/activation requirements and PR10's actual PR9 dev-merge/ancestry dependency.\n\nRetain concurrency10; truthful mutually exclusive lifecycle labels including agent:writing; complete question/option/answer recording; authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies; independent full-request recommended-choice resolution and routine-wait recovery; one global orchestrator at30-minute intervals while qualifying PRs are open, with idle exit; and self_host relevance limited to GitHub-agent functionality. Notifications remain limited to genuine approvals/questions, Telegram-requested feature status, dev merges, main merges and releases.\n\nPreserve genuine credentials/authentication/provenance/security holds, owner veto/cancel, current-row authority/CAS and operational freeze/drain. Preserve completed/cancelled operations without replaying them; do not restart a rollout or change frozen runtime/source under this amendment.\n\nEXPECTED SAFE TRANSITION\n\nKeep the old factual prerequisite hold throughout fresh planning and independent reassessment. The fresh reviewer must enumerate exactly PR47 as a removed condition, with the substantive full-task reason and this amendment's exact digest, only if the amended plan honestly makes it inherited baseline rather than a future external condition. Retain all still-required conditions.\n\nUse only the existing guarded amended-admission and exact-binding coordinator hold-to-renewal transition. A rejected reassessment, unavailable evidence, changed head/dev/task, separate hold/veto, failed persistence or stale CAS leaves work held. Do not manually edit request state, remove holds, force code, create successful checks or label the old verifier passed.\n\nThis amendment requests that supported reassessment; it does not pre-approve the resulting plan, code, merge, protected operation, deployment, visual acceptance or parent completion."],"decisions":[{"choice":"protected_conflict_repair_scope: Together in PR48 (Recommended)\nReason: The recorded request authorizes fixing GitHub-agent tooling issues reliably and repairing blockers while monitoring every qualifying PR through successful dev merge. Including the smallest pre-worker routing correction and fast regression in PR48 is a scope and ownership strategy consistent with that authorization; the request does not require a separate PR. Immutable dev-base instructions require small changes, independent review, preservation of authenticated parent context, and fresh exact-head protected approval. The choice expressly retains independent whole-plan/source review and all authority gates. Preserve PR48’s receiver foundation, current-dev safeguards and history, genuine missing-capability Pending states, every remaining source/runtime/native/visual/dependency gate, and the complete parent monitoring and operational requirements. Validate through GitHub under the private-worker restriction. This assessment establishes no failure cause, source acceptance, protected approval, deployment permission, hold release or parent completion.","questions":["1. How should the persistent protected-conflict routing repair be owned, while preserving PR #48’s receiver foundation, current-dev safeguards, and the complete parent task?\nTogether in PR48 (Recommended): Include the smallest pre-worker routing correction and fast regression with the protected conflict resolution; require fresh independent whole-plan/source review and all existing authority gates.\nSeparate automation leaf: Limit PR48 to reconciling receiver/current-dev source and history; commission a separately owned, independently reviewed routing repair PR and track both through successful dev merges."]}],"images":[],"plans":[{"approval_index":null,"id":"17836d3625858021625911e711d32a10c2ae31214def836e26b225db7c77c5cf","text":"# Reconcile PR48 with pinned dev and prevent protected-conflict retries\n\n## Summary and bindings\n\nCorrect PR48 head `573588880ad9d32afbcaa51e78844d0321a06a80` against assigned immutable dev `acc8989294a96c7b0b0d18dc257e2c810caa8764`. Preserve the complete receiver feature, authenticated parent task, chronological questions/options/answers, corrections, reviews and validation history.\n\nThe complete assigned feedback contains successful current-head fast CI, an unfinished independent review, three issue comments and no PR reviews. `fast_ci` contains no failed-job entries. These historical results do not validate the reconciled tree.\n\nKeep the independently resolved **Together in PR48** ownership choice. No additional user preference is required. Missing factual or authority evidence remains coordinator-owned.\n\n## Prerequisite reassessment before implementation\n\n- Retain the existing prerequisite hold during fresh planning and independent whole-plan reassessment.\n- Propose removing exactly **PR47’s future external dev-merge condition**, replacing it with mandatory preservation and verification of its inherited implementation. The catalogue records merge `04945ba5c60f15eead12ccefdbfb4b7932284dc9`; the coordinator must verify its inclusion in the assigned newer base using actual ancestry, signed head/task/branch and tree evidence.\n- Bind the reassessment to the authenticated amendment’s exact digest, current head/base/task, and old plan `ab38dc7de5a128b859d35550e540d2c82f7daed088258426f4f269f0d00a87aa`. Archive the original condition and failed verification unchanged. Never label the old verifier successful or PR47’s incomplete review approved.\n- Use only the existing guarded amended-admission and exact-binding hold-to-renewal transition. Rejection, unavailable evidence, changed bindings, separate holds, vetoes, stale CAS or persistence failure leave work held.\n- Authenticate any claimed session waiver from retained originals before applying it within its explicit scope. Quoted comments supply no approval or operational authority. This plan retains fresh substantive plan/source review and every unaffected protected or operational gate.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n**Reconcile both features with current dev.**\n\n- Reconstruct the merge in the permitted correction workspace and resolve conflicts without dropping either feature or unrelated dev changes.\n- In `.github/agent/controller.py`, retain receiver preparation and explicitly Pending publication interfaces. The final controller must protect both exact paths: `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_render.py` and `.github/workflows/agent-visual-profile.yml`. Preserve both rename-endpoint checks and reject similar adjacent paths.\n- Preserve PR47’s authority modules, transactional renewal APIs, tests and safeguards. Also preserve newer dev’s signed local-review admission, stale-discovery guards, workflow-specific validation recovery, and held read-only coordinator preparation.\n- Retain capture isolation, source-validation modes, diagnostic retention, workflow guards and publisher/dispatch semantics. Do not add publishing or dispatch capabilities.\n- Retain current dev’s Python 3.9–3.14 runtime profiles, Python 3.9 minimum constraints and SDK coverage. Preserve Python 3.8 public metadata/static syntax compatibility without restoring obsolete runtime jobs or the old all-matrix PR gate.\n- Combine operations-documentation and changelog additions. Preserve original evidence, rejections and additive metadata corrections. Record the routing repair in one owned changelog bullet without changing package versions.\n\n**Route protected conflicts before launching a worker.**\n\n- Inside `prepare`, immediately after the attempted merge and before collecting CI context or constructing a generic conflict prompt, inspect actual unresolved index paths for `conflict` tasks.\n- Snapshot the correction row before inspection. Use successful raw NUL-delimited Git output; preserve unusual filenames and deletion/rename conflict paths without line-based parsing.\n- Refuse sensitive paths such as `.git/`, `.connections` and `.env`. If unresolved paths cross the existing `.github/agent/` boundary or controller-workflow path, recheck current publication authority, including pinned dev, enrolled signed head, task context, vetoes and owner/coordinator holds.\n- Request correction planning through existing `require_correction(..., expected=snapshot)` semantics. Preserve current same-scope findings and concurrent replacement records.\n- Stop preparation before prompt/model launch. Only confirmed persistence may report correction queued; inspection, authority or persistence failures must refuse honestly.\n- Subsequent discovery must select the existing planned-correction route with unchanged parent context and separate plan review. Ordinary conflicts and clean protected inheritance retain existing behavior.\n- Preserve collector rejection, inherited-dev proof and publication guards. Do not loosen the generic conflict prompt.\n\nNo public API, receiver wire/schema, database schema, limit, credential permission or worker interface changes are required. Genuine live Gate/source-operation/current-row CAS/history and authenticated receiver-original retrieval remain Pending before effects.\n\n## Focused regression coverage and GitHub validation\n\nExtend `tests/repository/protected_conflicts.py` and its existing support fixtures:\n\n- Create real temporary-Git protected conflicts and prove preparation persists correction before prompt construction, model launch, collection or publication.\n- Verify restart durability and next-discovery correction selection with exact head/base/task bindings.\n- Cover ordinary conflicts, clean protected inheritance, deletion/rename cases, unusual NUL-delimited filenames and malformed/unavailable inspection.\n- Cover changed head/dev/task, unenrolled signatures, owner veto, coordinator holds, concurrent correction replacement and persistence failure. Assert no push, approval, hold release or lost findings.\n- Retain collector/publication rejection and inherited-dev tests. Test both exact protected paths, rename endpoints and adjacent-path negatives.\n- Retain receiver HTTP/Journal, capacity, identity, lifecycle, privacy, uncertain-receipt/no-repost and Pending-boundary coverage, alongside inherited authority, isolation, source-validation, local-review and read-only preparation regressions.\n\nExecute no candidate programs, tests, installs or renders in this planning/private-worker session or on the Pi. Validation runs through authorized isolated GitHub mechanisms:\n\n1. Obtain fresh independent whole-plan approval before source correction.\n2. Run focused regressions first, then required static/type/quality, canonical coverage and artifact checks. Preserve floors, assertions, failure signals and exact-head `fast-checks`.\n3. Retain the assigned baseline’s post-merge compatibility schedule; monitor its current Python/minimum/SDK profiles without making advisory integration a dev-merge gate.\n4. Obtain fresh complete composed-source/task/controller-closure review bound to the final head, dev base and task digest. Refresh affected evidence after changes.\n5. Verify signed publication and actual dev merge/ancestry through the existing managed route. Source publication or dev merge does not activate runtime changes.\n\n## Retained parent completion requirements\n\nContinue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs until every qualifying PR and successor actually merges successfully into dev. Preserve PR39/PR37, PR10/PR9 ancestry, exporter, producer–consumer and activation dependencies.\n\nPreserve all SQL Explorer repairs and all 46 scenes at 208×47 cells, with every geometry assertion and independent individual full 1280×800 PNG acceptance. This source-only correction supplies no visual acceptance.\n\nRetain concurrency 10, truthful mutually exclusive lifecycle labels including `agent:writing`, complete Q/options/A history, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies, independent recommendation resolution, routine-wait recovery, and one global 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit. Limit `self_host` relevance to GitHub-agent functionality and notifications to the recorded permitted categories.\n\nKeep credentials, provenance/security, owner veto/cancel, protected exact-head, whole-controller admission, compatible-consumer, main/source projection, native acceptance and operational freeze/drain gates intact. Preserve completed and cancelled operations without replaying them.\n"}],"producer_id":"local:ccd6409cda224ba59927524f54656265","questions":[],"replacements":[],"source":"user","starting_prompt":"implement it on your own if orchestator is not doing that","task_id":"ccd6409cda224ba59927524f54656265","version":2}